Subject: Re: Post-demo: SDK onboarding, auth routing, and intermittent 503s

Thanks Ben — reproducer details below. We are on the Node SDK and the failing code path is this snippet (we use the SDK wrapper):

// node SDK call (simplified)
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, timeout: 5000 }); // default 5s
const res = await client.rerank({
  queries: ["payment failure on mobile"],
  candidates: [["txn failed", "payment declined"]]
});

We attached the small log file. One of the failing entries includes request_id=fp-273 and the response we see client-side is an HTTP 503.

Per your suggestion we will spin a quick curl test and bump timeout to 20s; sharing results in the next message.

— Alex
